Decode keeps the json.Unmarshal error (wrapped with %w) only when errors.As finds a
*json.SyntaxError, and otherwise replaces it by errors.New "config: malformed
document". Expected: that opaque errors.New without chain; under the fmt.Errorf
"config: syntax error at byte %d: %w" link only values that may contain a
*json.SyntaxError (concrete *json.SyntaxError, wrappers around it, and Unresolved
entries, which no guard may remove). Concrete non-SyntaxError leaves and opaque json
errors must NOT appear directly under the fmt.Errorf link. Large because encoding/json
is followed; Unresolved field loads of unrelated Unwrap methods come from dynamic
Unwrap calls inside the stdlib.
-- args --
config/config.go:@decode
